From 802744d648abb8313cafa27d649077db92545f24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marcho78 <marcho78@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:58:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] board: nvidia: add SHIELD TV 2017 (P2894, darcy)

U-Boot runs as a second stage after NVIDIA's cboot, which starts it as
the kernel of an Android boot image and leaves the board set up.

The board code reads cboot's device tree and reports on screen what it
found: board revision, bootargs, memory banks, the HDMI framebuffer and
the ramdisk (with its CRC32, so a test image can confirm U-Boot did not
overwrite it).

- The console framebuffer is disabled unless cboot reports a surface big
  enough for 1080p inside DRAM: video probe clears the whole surface, so
  there is no safe default address. When used, it is handed on to the
  kernel as a simple-framebuffer and reserved.
- The ramdisk is booted only if it lies inside RAM and holds a whole FIT
  image. fdt_high is cleared first so bootm copies the device tree out of
  the FIT instead of growing it in place.
- With no console and no FIT to boot, the next boot carries the answer:
  the bootloader menu when cboot reported no framebuffer, Android when it
  reported one U-Boot could not use. The PMC is secure-only on the
  SHIELD, so the reboot reason goes through tegra_pmc_writel().
- No GPU/VPR programming, networking, EFI, storage-write commands or
  saved environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
